Note on the runtime license string: the compiled eBPF programs declare
"GPL" to the Linux kernel at load time (the DBGUARD_LICENSE macro). This is
a kernel requirement — several of the eBPF helper functions these programs
call are usable only by modules that declare a GPL-compatible license. The
declaration is about what the loaded program may call in the kernel; it does
not restrict your copyright license to the source, which remains GPL-2.0 OR
MIT as stated above.
